{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5291) to implement `cmd/uniq` covering srd028 requirements R1.1-R1.4 (Default deduplication only). This is part of the go-unix-utils project which reimplements GNU coreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/uniq/main.go` and `cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go`. The scope is limited to R1 (default deduplication) — R2 (output selection flags -d, -D, -u, -c), R3 (comparison options -i, -f, -s, -w), and R4 (exit codes) are explicitly NOT in this task's scope, though SIGPIPE handling is required by design decision D1.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `uniq` utility\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`guniq`)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` framework for side-by-side binary comparison\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for graceful SIGPIPE handling\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling test binaries\n   - Adjacent duplicate line suppression (not sorting — only adjacent duplicates)\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for consistent test behavior\n   - Manual argument parsing (no cobra for simple utilities)\n   - Copyright header requirement: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (hard limit from execution constitution E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines\n   - No git commands allowed — git managed by external orchestrator\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd028-uniq.yaml` (read)\n     - Full SRD for uniq; R1 (default dedup) is the focus for this task